WEBVTT

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.150
Somewhere in my heart,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.910
I seriously wished for something like this to happen.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.750
I don't care where...

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.460
I just wanna go to some foreign country.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.800
Me too.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.650
Somewhere nice and warm would be great!

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.060
Like an island in the south with lots of hot babes.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:45.340
One day, it dawned on me...

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:49.520
In this world, I'm neither a hero nor a sorcerer.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.530
Heck, I'm not even a player.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.360
I'm just an NPC villager.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.550
I'm fine with any place.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.770
Anywhere's better than here.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.750
I just wanted freedom from this meaningless reality.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:09.000
Escapism, delusions, Peter Pan syndrome...

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.130
It doesn't matter what you call it.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:16.930
Haven't you also wished for similar things in your life?

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:22.850
Fireworks?

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.110
It's four in the morning, man.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.660
That's just not right.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.940
It's pretty though.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:31.690
<i>Anywhere...</i>

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.490
Whoa! There goes a big one.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.370
Isn't it a little <i>too</i> big?

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:02.260
Alice in Borderland
Imawa no Kuni no Arisu

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.530
H-Huh?

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.990
Where the hell are we?

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.870
Am I... dreaming?

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.890
Is this for real?

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.330
Ready, set...

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.040
It expired yesterday...

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.870
This won't do! It's gone bad!

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.790
Alcoholic drinks and canned food are still good.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:16.460
There really isn't anyone around.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.920
We're just dreaming anyway.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.140
It's not a dream if it hurts, right?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.050
That doesn't work unless you pinch yourself!

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.600
Arisu?

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:30.690
Hey, what're you doing?

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:31.850
Hey, uh...
Hey, what're you doing?

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.700
Even though we're in this messed up situation...

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:42.490
I-Is it weird that I'm getting excited?

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.530
What?

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.290
To tell you the truth, me too, Arisu!

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.120
Chouta, not you too.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:59.000
Just look around. There aren't any parents here
telling you what to do, and no annoying teachers either.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.220
We are... free!

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.290
Fuck yeah!

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.530
Free! Free! Free! Free!

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.850
Maybe this is the freedom we've been longing for.
Free! Free! Free! Free!

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.560
Maybe this is the freedom we've been longing for.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.510
But still...

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.770
this is one long dream.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:18.980
Sure is.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.780
Isn't it lasting too long, though?

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:28.240
Arisu, Chouta, isn't it about time
you two think about this seriously?

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.700
This world...

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.410
could be real.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.800
I don't really mind

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.760
if this is reality.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:48.010
Whatever, man. We're finally enjoying ourselves—

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.840
What I'm saying isn't rocket science!

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.310
There's nothing wrong with being optimistic.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.980
I'm just saying you shouldn't
forget about your common sense.

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.420
There are...

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:10.190
other people here?

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.950
Hey, check that out.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.590
What's going on here?

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:34.860
See, Karube? I told you this is just a dream!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.780
How else would you explain all this?

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.650
Hot!

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:41.770
This is delicious!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.970
Oh, and over here is...

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.200
After you've entered the game,
<b>Survival Guide</b>

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.650
<b>Start
</b>After you've entered the game,
<b>Survival Guide</b>

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:56.660
After you've entered the game,
<b>Survival Guide</b>

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:00.450
Four entries confirmed.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:00.990
Festival entertainment?

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.470
The game will now begin.
Festival entertainment?

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:03.980
Where's the 4th person?
There is no way out.

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:04.460
Where's the 4th person?

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.370
Hey, this place is dangerous. We're leaving.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:09.650
Wait!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.550
Don't take another step.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.980
By the looks of it, you're first-timers.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:26.440
Keep thinking this place is a dream world or something,

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:27.980
and you'll end up dead.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.370
You get it now? It's too late.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:43.690
You all are already part of their game.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.210
Game?

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.720
The game's degree of difficulty is set to the three of clubs.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.320
TIME LEFT BEFORE
ENTRIES ARE CLOSED
Please draw one fortune slip per person.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:53.910
Please draw one fortune slip per person.

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:58.290
If everyone manages to draw
a fortune slip, the game is cleared.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:02.660
If even one of you hasn't drawn a fortune
slip by the time every lamp has gone off,

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.670
it's game over for all of you.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:09.140
Three of clubs, huh? It seems luck is still on my side.

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:11.070
Hey!

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.490
You better start talking! What is this "game"?

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:18.200
I have a name. It's Shibuki.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:21.810
Clubs mean that this game is relatively less dangerous.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.670
Plus, the degree of difficulty is three.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:27.200
If we work together and pay attention to the smallest of hints,

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.620
all of us might be able to leave here alive.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:35.350
Until we clear this game, we're bound by fate.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:36.890
Huh?

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.590
It's begun.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:43.730
Let's draw our fortune slips.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.150
Hey, w—

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:49.180
Wait a minute!

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:53.150
Those are the only rules?
What kinda game <i>is</i> this?

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:54.910
And I don't get the "game over" part.

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.670
You also said something about dying or living.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.240
You weren't actually serious, were you?

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.040
What the hell is this place anyway?!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.760
Can it already!

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:07.400
Instead of bombarding me with questions,
how about using your own head?

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:11.370
If you keep at it like that,
you won't last long in this place.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.370
I-Is this it?

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:22.110
So, what're we gonna do? Someone has to draw.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:28.530
There's no point in mulling over it.
If you don't want to, I'll go first.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:41.930
"You are the general! Person you're waiting for: will arrive. Direction: south is ideal."

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.120
What does this mean?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.770
I-Is that all?

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:46.920
Looks like it.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:52.630
You're really awesome, Karube!
You got "great blessing" at the first draw.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.950
All right! Me, next!

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.510
Shibuki, was it?

00:08:58.360 --> 00:08:59.290
Yes.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.480
This isn't your first time playing, right?

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:05.980
You've seen people die, haven't you?

00:09:06.970 --> 00:09:08.400
I have.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:12.320
Damn it, seriously? Small blessing?

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:16.200
What's this? There's a problem written here.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:22.350
The person who drew the fortune must answer the question written on it.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:26.120
If that's the case, I have a question for you.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:31.090
Why are you, someone who's already
survived a game, taking part in another one?

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:36.050
I just want to make sure if you're an ally or not.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:41.140
I'm in the same position as you guys are.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.770
What's gonna happen after this...

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.940
...is something you think about after getting out of here alive?

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.950
I get it. That will do for now.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:51.650
I got it, Arisu!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.400
The answer is more or less eighteen!

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:58.430
Come on. You can't answer with "more or less"!

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:03.290
Sorry, that is incorrect.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:06.070
Damn. I got it wrong.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.240
What'll happen if you get it wrong?

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:10.880
The one who answered incorrectly will be shot

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.420
with flaming arrows equal to the difference between the right and the wrong answers.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.710
What?

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.810
Did it say "flaming arrows"?

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:23.970
What's that?

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:43.030
Chouta!

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.470
Th-That was close.

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:52.380
If that first arrow hadn't knocked me down, I'd have been dead.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.750
They seriously shot with the intent to kill?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.630
Why would someone do this?

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:01.980
You understand the rules now?

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:03.100
I'm going next.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.080
Wh-What are you doing?

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.890
It's dangerous!
Didn't you see what just happened?!

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.390
<i>This</i>...

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.300
is dangerous?

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:17.110
What do you think'll happen if all the
lamps go off and we run out of time?

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:20.030
I'm sure you already have an idea.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:25.990
Face reality and rack your brains.
That is, if you don't want to die.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:32.210
<i>Huh? I... I-It's no good.</i>

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.520
I can't think straight.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:40.550
There's no way to approach a problem like this.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.880
It'll be tough to guess the right answer.

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:46.230
We should at least try to minimize the margin of error.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:49.740
Yeah. At the very least, the answer can't be less than one liter.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:53.270
<i>H-How...</i>

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:57.770
<i>How can you two accept this kind of reality?</i>

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.740
<i>I wanna go back...</i>

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.590
<i>I want to go back to that place right now.</i>

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.000
Arisu, Chouta, prepare yourselves.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:20.840
W-Wait a sec!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.260
The answer is "thirty"!

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:30.720
450?!

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.060
Sorry, that is incorrect.
450?!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.190
No way!

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.980
It doesn't matter where! Just hide!

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:44.820
<i>My legs are shaking and I can't move.</i>

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:49.760
<i>Am I gonna die here?</i>

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.580
If you want to live, man the fuck up, Arisu!

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.460
I know you can do it!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.710
You're my friend after all!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:14.770
Chouta!

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.520
Chou—

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:27.200
It hurts! It burns! I'm on fire!

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:29.280
Karube, Arisu!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.710
Karube! Chouta!

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.980
My adrenaline at full throttle!

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:48.910
This is starting to get fun!

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:53.100
I'm completely gung-ho right now, Arisu!

00:13:55.490 --> 00:13:59.940
<i>Amazing... You really are an amazing guy, Karube!</i>

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.690
If we don't pull it out right away, the wound'll set.

00:14:03.030 --> 00:14:04.150
It's gonna hurt, so bear with it.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.400
Please be gentle...
It's gonna hurt, so bear with it.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.330
Please be gentle...

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:08.480
Ow!

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:11.120
<i>I'm glad you're my friend.</i>

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.500
<i>If I'm with you, I might be able to accept this reality</i>.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:18.610
<i>If you can do it, so can I!</i>

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.490
What'd you draw?

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:25.880
Let me see!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:43.980
There's no way... we can answer this question.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:48.320
This is all messed up! There was never a chance from the start!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:50.620
Never a chance?

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.120
Arisu, I won't complain.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:59.600
My life is in your hands.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:06.630
It's hopeless. There's no way he can do it.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:08.590
<i>Think!</i>

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.210
<i>What'd everyone see and didn't see...</i>

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:14.970
Clubs mean that this game is relatively less dangerous.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:20.890
"You are the general! Person you're waiting for: will arrive. Direction: south is ideal."

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.090
What's this? There's a problem written here.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.900
It doesn't matter where! Just hide!

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:32.200
There was never a chance from the start!

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:36.580
I got it!

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.160
What?

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:39.790
The answer is...

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:41.750
6.9 billion!

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:44.200
A-Are you sure, Arisu?

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.630
More or less.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.250
More or less?!

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:53.180
Sorry, that is incorrect.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:57.630
You have a way out of this, don't you...

00:15:58.600 --> 00:15:59.820
Arisu?

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.140
Everyone, listen up.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.140
The arrows will come from the north.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.510
How'd you know?

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:06.770
The fortune slips said so.

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:09.800
There was no way to answer this question.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:13.240
That's right. There was never a chance from the start!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:17.320
Getting the correct answer is not how you clear this game.

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:22.120
They said we should answer the questions,
but they didn't say that we will clear the game if we do so.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:27.590
Noticing these hints is the key to this game.

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:32.410
The direction from where the arrows would come was already written on the fortune slips.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:36.430
First, west. Next, east.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.720
And now, from the north.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.220
<b>North is inauspicious.
And now, from the north.</b>

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.180
There's no way it's that simple!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:45.230
It <i>is</i> that simple.
They just made it difficult to notice.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:48.960
The order in which the fortune slips came out was probably also preset.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.730
This is that kind of a game!

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:53.950
Yeah, it was written on my fortune slip.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:57.160
"Direction: south is ideal!"

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.870
Now that we know that...

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:05.210
Run until your lungs burst!

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.340
Damn, that's hot!

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:19.470
We're almost there!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:23.430
There's no way we're dying after getting this far!

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:25.140
We're here!

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:27.090
An old well?

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:28.800
We might be safe inside here—

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.740
It's been filled?

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.770
<i>How can this be?</i>

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.700
<i>Did I overlook something?</i>

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:48.000
I'm also starting to understand...

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:51.720
how these guys planned this game!

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:53.250
It won't hold much longer!

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:56.720
I am...

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:03.720
Karube Daikichi!

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:17.570
Why's something like this underneath the shrine?

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:23.150
Congratulations. You've cleared the game.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:28.700
You all drew fortune slips and managed to survive.

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:37.010
How's that, you bastards?

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.880
Miss! We survived thanks to you!

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:42.930
G-Get off!
Miss! We survived thanks to you!

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:47.440
We're alive!

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:00.970
A visa?

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:04.650
That shows how many days you can stay here in Borderland.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:06.580
Borderland?

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:10.910
That's the name of this place we're in right now.

00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:17.800
Shibuki-san said...

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:22.510
that what she's about to tell us is something she heard from the previous participants.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:25.230
Just rumors and speculations.

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:27.470
It's nothing concrete.

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:32.690
There are a lot of other people besides us here in Borderland.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:35.490
They participate in games which are held after sundown.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.650
Once you clear a game,

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:41.610
you'll receive a visa and your period of stay is extended.

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:46.260
The game we cleared today was the three of clubs.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:48.480
Our visa will expire in three days.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:57.440
What's wrong, Chouta?

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.170
S-Someone's there...

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:05.180
Are you also a participant?

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:09.100
I don't want to take part anymore... ever again.

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:13.480
I haven't told you what'd happen
if your visa were to expire, have I?

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:17.480
My friends are all dead.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:18.440
I've had enough.

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:22.400
I won't participate in games anymore!

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.080
H-Hey!

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:26.660
It's time.

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:38.670
This is what happens when your visa expires.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.230
Freedom from this meaningless reality.

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:43.630
Escapism...

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:49.060
Haven't you also wished for similar things in your life?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.850
My wish was granted...

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:57.620
and here I am.

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:33.620
<b>What if I... <i>we</i> are somehow
being tested here in Borderland?</b>

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:39.670
<b>If I'm "it" in tag,
should I really be thinking like that?</b>

00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:46.720
<b>That's why... it'll be more
meaningful if we bet our lives <i>here</i>!</b>

00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:54.840
Next time on <i>Alice in Borderland</i>,

00:22:54.840 --> 00:23:00.090
"2nd Game: Five of Spades."
